    "modifiedAt": "2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "bo_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -444
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Breakout\n\nClick the preview to start, then move the mouse left and right to steer the paddle; click again to launch each ball. Break every brick to go up a level (the ball gets faster); three balls, then click to play again. Until you click, the game plays itself.\n\nHow it works: the game is state, kept from frame to frame by Write → Read pairs (a Read at the start of the flow gives what its Write stored at the end of the last frame), wired with visual nodes only. Turns (open it with a double-click) decides when a game starts and when the ball launches. Ball moves the ball by its velocity and steers the paddle. Bricks tests the ball against all 60 bricks at once with Hit Test and remembers which still stand. Next turn counts lives, score and level, and puts the ball back on the paddle. Bounce bounces the ball off the walls, the paddle and broken bricks. HUD draws the score, the balls left and the message. Sparks fly from broken bricks.",
        "width": 460,
        "height": 380
      }
    },
